11. Real-world networking troubleshooting
Imagine your Spark worker cannot communicate with the Hadoop NameNode.

Follow this basic troubleshooting order:
1. Check the interface
   ip link
   ip addr
   
   
   Is the interface up? Does it have an IP address?
2. Check routing
   ip route
   
   
   Is the required route available?
3. Check connectivity
   ping -c 4 <NameNode-IP>
   
   
   Can the worker reach the NameNode?
4. Check DNS
   getent hosts namenode-hostname
   
   
   Does the hostname resolve correctly?
5. Check the service and port
   ss -tulpen
   
   
   Is the required application service listening on its expected port?

This helps narrow down whether the issue is related to the interface, route, DNS or service.

